<title>THAILAND: Thai govt to cut 57 bln baht off 1997/98 budget.</title>
<headline>Thai govt to cut 57 bln baht off 1997/98 budget.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai government said on Friday it will cut its 1997/98 (October-September) budget by 57 billion baht ($1.84 billion) to 925 billion baht.</p>
<p>Deputy Finance Minister Chaturon Chaisaeng said the cut would trim the budget for the 1997/98 financial year from 982 billion baht. The new figure is the same level as the budget for the current 1996/97 fiscal year.</p>
</text>
